From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 16:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hal-droid: build the pipeline off the luna-service2 handler thread

Bringing droidcamsrc to PLAYING blocks, and startCapture() runs on the
luna-service2 handler thread, so the block also stops that thread's main loop
dispatching anything else. A plain gst-launch reaches PLAYING with an identical
pipeline on this hardware while the camera service never does, and the calling
context is the most visible remaining difference between the two.

Run the build on a thread of its own and join it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS Halium-specific]
---
--- a/src/plugins/hal/droid/droid_camera_plugin.cpp	2026-09-05 10:09:55.286081813 +0200
+++ b/src/plugins/hal/droid/droid_camera_plugin.cpp	2026-09-05 10:09:55.304642930 +0200
@@ -331,7 +331,19 @@
     constexpr int kAttempts = 3;
     for (int attempt = 1; attempt <= kAttempts; attempt++)
     {
-        if (buildPipeline())
+        /* Build on a thread of our own rather than on the luna-service2
+         * handler thread we were called from. Bringing droidcamsrc to PLAYING
+         * blocks, and doing that on the service's main loop stops it dispatching
+         * anything else - including whatever droidmedia may be waiting on. A
+         * plain gst-launch reaches PLAYING with the identical pipeline, and the
+         * calling context is the most visible thing that differs. */
+        bool built = false;
+        {
+            std::thread worker([this, &built]() { built = buildPipeline(); });
+            worker.join();
+        }
+
+        if (built)
         {
             if (attempt > 1)
                 PLOGI("droid pipeline started on attempt %d", attempt);
